WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.470
In 1970, Britain passed a law saying women
must get equal pay for the same work.

2
00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:10.840
In 2025, a woman was chosen
as Archbishop of Canterbury,

3
00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:13.000
to lead the Church of England.

4
00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:17.100
Paul wrote that in Christ there
is neither male nor female.

5
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.950
Yet in some churches, only
men may ever be priests.

6
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.260
So if a faith teaches that
women and men are equal,

7
00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:27.250
why can't women lead worship everywhere?

8
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:32.260
In this mission, you'll pin down the difference
between prejudice and discrimination.

9
00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:35.770
Then you'll follow a timeline of
women's ministry in the churches,

10
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.940
and see where it stops.

11
00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:43.180
Your mission: find out why faiths that
teach equality may still limit who leads

12
00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:43.960
worship.
